commit 36efd3970f6931221e5749539c93f218e9147dba
Author: Bruce Guenter <bruce@untroubled.org>
Date:   Fri Jul 10 16:24:08 2020 -0600

    fix(loki sink): Set a proper default for the batch buffer initialization (#3016)

    * Use BatchSize in Buffer instead of breaking it down

    * Set a default event buffer size for the loki sink

    The loki sink uses VecBuffer but did not set a default for the maximum
    number of events. When unset, the default number of events is
    `usize::max_value()`. Further, VecBuffer creates an array based on this
    maximum number of events. This causes a run time error due to the vector
    size being too large for memory.

    Signed-off-by: Bruce Guenter <bruce@timber.io>

